/volumes/

# The drill's own logs. Kept ON PURPOSE — `drill-run.sh` tees here because the
# journal only ever recorded "exit 1, and it said nothing", and `.log.1` holds
# the run before this one because `tee` truncates and a weekly drill overwrote
# the evidence of the failure nobody had read yet (#1471).
#
# Ignored rather than committed: they are a machine's account of its own run, and
# odin is the only host that has them. Untracked-but-not-ignored made a clean
# checkout read as three modified files for ever, which spends the signal that
# says somebody edited a script in place.
/drill-run.log
/drill-run.log.1
/drill-seed-fast.log
